    "proved": "Relative-envelope membership of a separated sum on a finite product is equivalent to membership of each coordinate in its own relative class. For arbitrary admissible curve backgrounds, zero-obstacle ordinary/ideal equality, equality of polar and atomic curvatures, relative membership in the ideal reference and equality at every smooth product obstacle are equivalent. Mixed obstacles, zero-area coordinates and zero-volume models are included. The same criterion holds through the nonnegative nonclosed auxiliary coefficient and unit-divisor extension.",
    "mechanism": "Add coordinate stretching competitors to obtain product membership; genuine coordinate restrictions and constant corrections give its converse. The separated zero-obstacle projections identify envelope equality factorwise, and the complete curve criterion and ideal obstacle reprojection give arbitrary mixed-obstacle equality. On the auxiliary extension, slices give the ordinary projection, preservation of ideals gives the ideal projection, and the same added competitors prove relative membership directly. A prose ending restores the missing automatic proof-ending symbol in the unchanged smooth geodesic equation.",
    "existing_proof_editorial_repair": "Chapter16 Schur proof ends with the invariant scalar identity interpreted in prose, restoring its QED; its statement, formulas and labels are unchanged.",
    "retained_boundary": "The all-obstacle criterion concerns separated curve potentials and their specified auxiliary/unit-divisor extensions. It does not factor mixed-obstacle envelopes or settle unrestricted higher-dimensional zero-volume implications."
